Toltec aphorism concerning the appearance of Crows in dreams with words reminding the dreamer to note the direction of flight.

**East**: Represents **Education** and the **Scholar**, who is preoccupied with sobriety and the **Mastery of Awareness**. It symbolizes vision, new beginnings, and the rising sun.

**North**: Represents **Politics** and the **Man of Action**, who is preoccupied with action and **materialization**. It symbolizes strength, stillness, and the physical expression of the Fourfold Purpose.

**South**: Represents **Religion** and warmth, symbolizing passion, nurturing, and the **warm night wind**. It is associated with growth, emotion, and the light of the New Testament.

**West**: Represents **Medicine** and the **Man Behind the Scenes**, who is concerned with erasing personal history and the **Mastery of Intent**. It symbolizes the setting sun, death, introspection, and **liberation through the power of intent**.

The **Center** is encompassed by the fifth pillar, **Science** (depicted as a comet), which circles and contains the four-fold pillars.
